## Provider Hardening
- Timeouts and retries/backoff on 429/5xx; fail‑soft partial results.
- Tavily as primary; LinkedIn/Diffbot only if keys exist and needed (e.g., poor answer quality).
- Caching (optional but recommended): in-memory/Redis by `(company, domain, question, max_results)` with TTL; metric: cache hit%.

## Normalization Rules
- Always include: `company`, `summary[]`, `results[]`, `total_sources`.
- `results[].sources[]` contain `{title,url}` only (no sensitive blobs).
- `extracted_people[]`: `{name, title, linkedin_url?, source_url?}`
- `summary[]`: 3–6 concise bullets; `key_insights[]`: actions (e.g., "Prioritize CIO outreach").

## Security & Guardrails
- Input sanitation for `company`, `domain` (length caps, allowed chars).
- Respect provider rate limits; log latency and errors (no PII).
- Saving to CRM behind a UI toggle + role check; attach JSON only if needed.

